# gpu_frame_00000_*.png and gpu_frame_00030_*.png in this directory come from this run (debug
# build), compared with the same run with --image-targets cpu (Rerun's screenshot and picking
# readbacks):
# - color: byte-identical (cmp), and for frame 0 byte-identical to
#   docs/evidence/stereo_frame_000_color.png (Metal, CPU path).
# - depth, raw f32 (--raw-depth, 1920000 values per frame): 24069 values differ, by at most
#   3 ULPs (1.8e-7). The 8-bit depth PNG differs where such a step crosses a gray level; the CPU
#   run's depth PNG is byte-identical to docs/evidence/stereo_frame_000_depth.png.
# - with MVK_CONFIG_FAST_MATH_ENABLED=0 for both runs: color PNG, depth PNG and raw depth are
#   byte-identical. The difference is Metal's fast-math division in the depth conversion of
#   eye_output.wgsl; the picking depth itself is the same.

