## 3. Khronos validation layer

# Homebrew vulkan-validationlayers 1.4.363, VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS=VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation,
# VK_KHRONOS_VALIDATION_REPORT_FLAGS=error,warn, messages to a file. Run 1 with --image-targets gpu
# and with --image-targets cpu, and the viewer against the stub (--frames 200 --quit-when-done,
# 200 frames shown, every write-back accepted, every semaphore consumed): each reports only
# VUID-StandaloneSpirv-None-10684, 20 times, at shader module creation, from the SPIR-V naga
# generates for Rerun's shaders. The output pass's shader adds no message.

## 4. Per-frame time, picking readback against GPU depth (release builds, relative only)

# Same machine, scene (log-test-scene 600), head motion (still), 300 shown frames per run, three
# runs per row, from the viewer's own summary line: ms/frame is 1000 over the mean frames shown
# per second, begin-to-show the mean of the runs' averages. The image-sink rows also
# include --image-targets gpu's own readback of the sink's targets with a wait for the device
# every frame, the same on both sides. The stub serves 64x64 per eye only.
#
# setup                         readback depth            GPU depth
#                               ms/frame  begin-to-show   ms/frame  begin-to-show
# image sink, 960x1000 per eye  28.8      21.7 ms         16.6      9.9 ms
# image sink, 1832x1920 per eye 61.6      54.5 ms         45.2      38.3 ms
# qaros-stub, 64x64 per eye     18.2      10.1 ms         9.7       1.6 ms
#
# Apple GPU through MoltenVK; these numbers do not predict an NVIDIA GPU on Windows.

## 5. Depth at a lower resolution (--depth-scale-down N, release builds, relative only)

# Debug build, run 1's settings plus --depth-scale-down 2 --raw-depth, against run 1 with
# --image-targets cpu: color PNGs of frames 0 and 30 byte-identical; every depth value equals the
# smallest forward depth of its 2x2 block in the CPU run (the nearest), largest difference 1.8e-7.
# Under the validation layer: only VUID-StandaloneSpirv-None-10684, 20 times, as in section 3.
#
# Timing as in section 4 (image sink only; the stub's depth is always the color's size), another
# build of the same code, so divisor 1 is measured again:
#
# depth divisor                 960x1000 per eye          1832x1920 per eye
#                               ms/frame  begin-to-show   ms/frame  begin-to-show
# 1                             16.7      9.9 ms          44.7      38.0 ms
# 2                             15.6      8.9 ms          39.3      32.3 ms
# 4                             15.8      8.9 ms          33.7      26.8 ms
#
# The image sink also reads its depth targets back every frame, smaller with a larger divisor, so
# these rows overstate what the renderer itself saves. What lower-resolution depth saves in
# QAROS (encoding, network) cannot be measured here.
